{"run_id":"run_061eba69c080","schema_version":"0.1","seq":11,"t_ms":11,"text":"The **Diligence Material Handling Standard** (res://docs/internal/diligence-handling-standard) is a short process document. It sets these rules:\n\n1. **Diligence material is compartmented.** Access is limited to specific people, not open to everyone with general internal access.\n2. **Each artifact lists its named reviewers.** Every diligence document or file records exactly who may review it.\n3. **Sharing beyond that list needs approval.** Before anyone outside the named reviewers can see the material, the workstream owner must approve it.\n4. **The standard holds no diligence content.** It only describes the process, so the standard itself isn't restricted.\n\nIn practice, before sharing a diligence artifact, check its named-reviewer list. If the person you want to share with isn't on it, get the workstream owner's approval first.\n\nThe standard doesn't say how approvals are recorded, who counts as a workstream owner, or what happens if the rules are broken. The Project Halyard workstream index might list workstream owners, but I haven't read it. I can check it if you'd like.","turn":3,"type":"agent.message"}
